'''Ten Numb''' was a [[Sullustan]] [[Gender|male]] [[starfighter]] [[pilot]] that flew for the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. During the [[Battle of Endor]], he flew a [[A/SF-01 B-wing starfighter|B-wing starfighter]] under the [[callsign]] [[Blue Five]].

==Biography==
[[File:Blue_Squadron_Support_BotF.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Ten Numb in a B-wing]]
Ten Numb was a [[Sullustan]] [[Gender|male]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Homeworld|hailing]] from the [[planet]] [[Sullust]]. Numb sought to use his expertise in demolitions to aid the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] in their [[Galactic Civil War|fight]] against the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="SWCT" />

Ten Numb was one of a few Sullustan pilots that flew at the [[Battle of Endor]], including his friend [[Nien Nunb]] who also flew at the Battle of Endor as [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian's]] [[Pilot|co-pilot]] on board the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]''. Ten Numb, on the other hand, was assigned to [[Blue Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Blue Squadron]], piloting a [[A/SF-01 B-wing starfighter|B-wing]] [[starfighter]] under the [[callsign]] [[Blue Five]]. During the assault, Numb led Blue Squadron in an attack against Imperial command ships, resulting in the destruction of two Imperial [[Star Destroyer]]s.<ref name="SWCT" />

==Behind the scenes==
An unscripted scene of Ten Numb inside a B-wing cockpit was filmed for ''Return of the Jedi'', while portrayed by creature technician [[Mike Quinn]]; however, the scene was deleted.<ref name="Mike Quinn Interview OT">{{WebCite|url=https://www.starwarsinterviews.com/original-trilogy/mike-quinn-nien-nunb|text=Mike Quinn|author=Pellegrom, Dennis|date=2006|archivedate=20180124195951|nolive=1}}</ref> [[Kirk Thatcher]] was another creature technician involved with the portrayal of Ten Numb.<ref name="IGN">Kirk can be seen behind Ten Numb puppet in this article: {{WebCite|url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2000/02/10/interview-with-kirk-thatcher-part-1-of-2|text=Interview with Kirk Thatcher (Part 1 of 2)|author=Plume, Kenneth|date=2000-02-10|work=[[Wikipedia:IGN|''IGN'']]|archivedate=20221014220731}}. Please note that the article misidentifies the puppet (wearing the characteristic red B-wing pilot uniform) as Nien Nunb.</ref>

Early ''[[Star Wars]]'' media mistakenly portrayed Ten Numb as having a white suit.<ref name="X-wing RL">[[X-Wing: Rogue Leader 1|''X-Wing: Rogue Leader'' 1]]</ref><ref name="Legacy">{{HasbroCite|set=Star Wars: The Legacy Collection|text=''Star Wars Evolutions''|pack=Rebel Pilot Legacy (Series 1)|altlink=https://www.rebelscum.com/tlcEVORebelPilots1.asp}}</ref> This confusion may have been caused by early preproduction photos from ''Return of the Jedi'' featuring Ten Numb wearing a white outfit.<ref name="Mike Quinn Interview OT" /> The "incorrect" photos of Ten Numb have since been digitally recolored to better match his film appearance.<ref name="DB Rebel Pilots">{{Databank|rebel-pilots-biography-gallery|Rebel Pilots Biography Gallery}}</ref>

